1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,040
You failed.

2
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:07,780
Instead of bringing the Uranus Queen to us as instructed,

3
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:09,380
you allowed her to awaken.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,280
I apologize, Master.

5
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:14,720
You have failed us for the last time, Beta.

6
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,900
Those insects have never come close to finding the synops.

7
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:20,920
After several thousand years, what purpose does she serve?

8
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:23,640
The electronic warfare class Angeloid is obsolete.

9
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:25,700
Wait! Don't do that!

10
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:27,480
I'll get her next time, I promise!

11
00:00:27,480 --> 00:00:30,280
What can you possibly do to take down the Uranus Queen

12
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:31,360
now that she's awakened?

13
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:33,780
Wait a moment.

14
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:37,200
I have an idea.

15
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:57,260
I am so horrifyingly bored,

16
00:00:57,260 --> 00:00:58,200
being up here.

17
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:00,060
Entertain me.

18
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:03,060
Whatever you ask of me, Master!

19
00:01:03,060 --> 00:01:09,120
I imagine that.

20
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:20,640
During the age of discovery,

21
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:24,340
there was a setback aboard the ship on which Columbus was sailing.

22
00:01:24,820 --> 00:01:27,260
His sailors were having doubts about their long journey

23
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:29,320
and in their despair attempted a mutiny.

24
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:31,320
I see.

25
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:33,320
So Columbus lied to them.

26
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:35,320
He entered a much shorter journey into the ship's log

27
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:38,320
than the real figures of which he was perfectly aware.

28
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:41,320
Having believed these figures, the men continued their journey,

29
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:44,320
and that crew is said to have eventually discovered the new world.

30
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:46,320
You could actually say...

31
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:49,320
You could say it's a tale that started with a lie.

32
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:52,320
A tale of the discovery of the new world.

33
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:55,320
Nikako, just what are you doing?

34
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:57,320
Well, clearly I'm your assistant.

35
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:59,320
Weren't you looking for a new one?

36
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:02,320
I figured you'd be lonely all by yourself,

37
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:04,320
so I thought I'd come help you out some.

38
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:08,320
I'm pretty number three at your service.

39
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:18,320
It's the perfect weather for a barbecue.

40
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:20,320
Holy crap!

41
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:23,320
This place is swimming with people.

42
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:25,320
Over here!

43
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:29,320
A few of my men are holding down a spot for us nearby.

44
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:30,320
And look!

45
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:32,320
In the shade!

46
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:37,320
Hey, Tomiki?

47
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:39,320
Nymph hasn't come back yet, has she?

48
00:02:39,320 --> 00:02:40,320
No, not yet.

49
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:43,320
She's probably back visiting her homeland up in the sky.

50
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:44,320
Jeez, what a load.

51
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:46,320
She drops in out of nowhere then vanishes into thin air.

52
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:48,320
We should start setting everything up.

53
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:51,320
Hang on, where's Icarus?

54
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:02,320
Don't do that, lady! You'll break it!

55
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:03,320
Icarus!

56
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:05,320
What are you doing over here, you idiot?

57
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:06,320
Sorry about that, sir.

58
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:08,320
I'll pay for the whole thing.

59
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:10,320
How much are we talking about?

60
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:12,320
No freaking way!

61
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:13,320
This is huge!

62
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:15,320
This is that legendary DVD,

63
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:18,320
the ridiculously perverted one with all the bouncy goodness!

64
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:21,320
The Age of Warring Boobs, G-Cup Rebellion!

65
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:24,320
It's nothing short of a miracle that I found this sucker here!

66
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:25,320
Of all places!

67
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:27,320
I'll, uh...

68
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:28,320
I'll take this.

69
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:31,320
No tears!

70
00:03:36,320 --> 00:03:38,320
Excuse me, Master.

71
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:41,320
I'm sorry that happened.

72
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:47,320
I need to act normal.

73
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:50,320
I have to find a way to be more like the humans I know.

74
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:54,320
Little Miss Weapon of Death!

75
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:56,320
But how?

76
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:58,320
How do humans act?

77
00:03:58,320 --> 00:04:00,320
I can't believe you said that!

78
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:01,320
Oh, come on.

79
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:02,320
It's only human to lie.

80
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:04,320
That's terrible!

81
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:05,320
So you've lied to me.

82
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:10,320
To act human is to lie.

83
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:16,320
Welcome back, Tomaki!

84
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:17,320
And Icarus!

85
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:19,320
The meat will be done soon!

86
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:22,320
To act human is to lie.

87
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:23,320
Um, Sohara?

88
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:24,320
Yeah?

89
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:25,320
What's up?

90
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:27,320
I just wanted you to know that I hate you.

91
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:31,320
No one thinks you're cute.

92
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:34,320
In fact, everyone thinks you're quite unattractive.

93
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:37,320
You appear to be kind, but you're actually a very violent person.

94
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:39,320
But why?

95
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:42,320
I also think you're just a little too skinny.

96
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:44,320
And that's a bad thing?

97
00:04:44,320 --> 00:04:46,320
Anyway, I just wanted to let you know.

98
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:49,320
Those are the reasons I hate you as much as I do.

99
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:59,320
The new world doesn't exist, Sugata.

100
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:01,320
And Prez, you're...

101
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:02,320
I'm what?

102
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:07,320
You're a very nice person.

103
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:08,320
Oh, stop.

104
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:10,320
You're making me blush.

105
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:11,320
I don't get it!

106
00:05:11,320 --> 00:05:13,320
That's the opposite of what you said about me!

107
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:18,320
And as for you, Tomoki, I don't want to be with you anymore.

108
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:21,320
I don't want to be with you anymore.

109
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:33,320
Is this crap the best you can cook?

110
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:35,320
I thought I was a good person!

111
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:38,320
You two are pretty lucky to be able to get drunk off soda.

112
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:40,320
We're still not even close to old enough to drink,

113
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:42,320
so we have to find something, don't we?

114
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:45,320
I don't think it's something to be this upset over.

115
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:46,320
I just can't help it.

116
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:49,320
No one has ever talked to me like that before.

117
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:51,320
Icarus is such a beating!

118
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:55,320
Well then, by all means, drink yourself stupid.

119
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:57,320
Icarus didn't vanish,

120
00:05:57,320 --> 00:05:59,320
and Icarus doesn't want to be with me anymore.

121
00:05:59,320 --> 00:06:01,320
This sucks.

122
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:05,320
Everybody's just doing whatever the hell they want.

123
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:06,320
Damn!

124
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:09,320
I need something to take my mind off this crap,

125
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:12,320
cause if not, it's gonna drive me nuts!

126
00:06:14,320 --> 00:06:17,320
The takoyaki you're serving looks like poop on a stick.

127
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:20,320
You've got a beautiful thick head of hair.

128
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:23,320
Your baby is uglier than you are.

129
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:26,320
Finally, I'm acting human.

130
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:31,320
You look like you're having a good time, Alpha.

131
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:32,320
Hello, Nymph.

132
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:36,320
What are you doing here?

133
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:39,320
Wanna do me a favor and disable your Artemis lock-on?

134
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:42,320
Cause if you don't, those missile alarms ringing in my head

135
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:45,320
are gonna drive me up the nearest wall.

136
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:47,320
I'm not here to tell people who you really are.

137
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:48,320
Nothing like that.

138
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:50,320
And it's not like I could ever beat you in battle,

139
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:52,320
so you can relax a bit, girl.

140
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:53,320
Don't worry.

141
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:56,320
I just wanna see what's happening on my soap opera.

142
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:58,320
Maybe hang around a little longer, you know?

143
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:00,320
Sure.

144
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:03,320
Tell me, Alpha.

145
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:07,320
Don't you think you're a bit subservient to your new master down here?

146
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:09,320
These stupid bugs are just trash to us.

147
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:10,320
They're nothing.

148
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:12,320
I still don't get what you're trying to do.

149
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:15,320
But unless you wanna destroy your relationship with him,

150
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:18,320
don't even mention what happened between you and me.

151
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:23,320
Hmph.

152
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:24,320
Fooled her completely.

153
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:28,320
She has no clue the only reason I'm here is to take her back.

154
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:31,320
Peace Stealth System, activate.

155
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:33,320
I will follow my master's orders.

156
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:36,320
Even though I've got no way to outstrip her firepower,

157
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:39,320
I'm gonna take her back into the sky with me.

158
00:07:39,320 --> 00:07:43,320
But to achieve that, I gotta do something else first.

159
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:50,320
I'm taking her precious master hostage.

160
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:52,320
See how she likes that.

161
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:53,320
So sorry, Alpha.

162
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:56,320
You think that's enough to keep out of sight?

163
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:58,320
Because I can see you.

164
00:07:58,320 --> 00:07:59,320
Wait!

165
00:07:59,320 --> 00:08:00,320
What?

166
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:02,320
How is this possible?

167
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:05,320
You gotta try harder to keep from my prying eyes.

168
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:08,320
I can see freaking everything.

169
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:11,320
That's the stuff, baby.

170
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:12,320
Yeah, do it!

171
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:14,320
What are you doing?

172
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:16,320
What does it look like I'm watching people do it?

173
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:19,320
Nothing like a live show to cheer me up.

174
00:08:19,320 --> 00:08:21,320
Since I can't afford the DVD...

175
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:22,320
Wait.

176
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:23,320
Who's there?

177
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:24,320
Nope?

178
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:29,320
What are those two people doing?

179
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:32,320
It looks like the woman is taking off her clothes.

180
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:33,320
Don't look!

181
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:35,320
And where the hell have you been, huh?

182
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:36,320
You've freaking vanished into thin air!

183
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:38,320
You can't pull that crap!

184
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:39,320
Whatever.

185
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:40,320
Who cares?

186
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,320
I care, dummy!

187
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:43,320
If you're gonna leave, at least let me know first.

188
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:46,320
You have any idea how much I've been worrying about you?

189
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:47,320
You've been worried?

190
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:48,320
Of course I have!

191
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:55,320
I mean, sure, you're a self-centered freeloader, but that doesn't mean you can just disappear without telling anybody!

192
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:57,320
Yeah, okay.

193
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:58,320
Hang on!

194
00:08:58,320 --> 00:09:03,320
I'm here to take him hostage, not get ordered around.

195
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:05,320
What am I doing listening to him?

196
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:06,320
Good.

197
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:09,320
Now, as punishment, you have to do everything I tell you today.

198
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:10,320
Understand me?

199
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:11,320
Now, let's go.

200
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:12,320
You're coming with me.

201
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,320
Uh, no!

202
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:14,320
Wait!

203
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:27,320
So, what are you doing again?

204
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:28,320
Huh?

205
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:29,320
Can't you tell by looking?

206
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:31,320
There's a flea market going on.

207
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,320
I'm setting up a booth.

208
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:36,320
I need that DVD, but I'm flat broke.

209
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:39,320
Therefore, my brilliant plan is to sell off all my old crap.

210
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:41,320
And then the boobies will be mine!

211
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:44,320
I'm a freaking genius!

212
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:47,320
You think this junk will sell?

213
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:48,320
Maybe.

214
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:50,320
That's why I needed someone to help me out.

215
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:52,320
So, here's what you do.

216
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:54,320
Get out there and attract some customers.

217
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:55,320
What?

218
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:57,320
What are the two of you up to?

219
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:59,320
Um, hey, guys!

220
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,320
Nymph!

221
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:01,320
Good to see you again!

222
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:03,320
Icarus told us you'd come back.

223
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:05,320
We would have missed you if you hadn't.

224
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:06,320
I'm so glad.

225
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:08,320
So, welcome back!

226
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:10,320
Yeah, thanks, I guess.

227
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:12,320
It looks like you're running a booth.

228
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:15,320
But I honestly don't think any of this stuff is gonna sell.

229
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:16,320
You don't know that!

230
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,320
Oh, come on.

231
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:19,320
This could be fun.

232
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:21,320
I've always wanted to try my hand at retail.

233
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:24,320
Hey, Icarus, let's you and I run a booth!

234
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:27,320
Come one, come all!

235
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:31,320
Get your bellies filled with Icarus' delicious lunches!

236
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:34,320
Our shop is an enormous success, Icarus!

237
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:36,320
The two of us make a great combo!

238
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:38,320
If you say so, Sahara.

239
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:41,320
So, uh, all that stuff you said to me before,

240
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:43,320
you know, about hating me and all?

241
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:45,320
That's right, I totally hate you.

242
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:48,320
That's what I thought!

243
00:10:48,320 --> 00:10:53,320
There's your everyday Tommy gun,

244
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:56,320
or your Colt M1911 pistol.

245
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:59,320
But of course, they're all non-working replicas.

246
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:02,320
Aw, damn it.

247
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:04,320
Jerks are stealing all of my customers.

248
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:07,320
Well, Sagata, not so much, of course.

249
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:10,320
Nymph, you're gonna have to help me out somehow.

250
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:13,320
I want that DVD more than anything!

251
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:15,320
I'm not doing anything else.

252
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:16,320
Guess I'll help.

253
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:17,320
Really? You will?

254
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:20,320
When you get the DVD, can I watch it too?

255
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:22,320
I don't know.

256
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:27,320
Tell you what, instead, if we make some decent cash,

257
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:29,320
I'll buy you whatever you want.

258
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:31,320
Whatever I want?

259
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:33,320
Suppose that could work.

260
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:35,320
And I just gotta help you, right?

261
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:37,320
Sure, that sounds easy enough.

262
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:38,320
Thanks a million, Nymph.

263
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:41,320
You know, this stuff you're trying to sell is pretty crappy.

264
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:44,320
Why don't you open up a food booth like Alpha did?

265
00:11:44,320 --> 00:11:46,320
Like Okonomiyaki, maybe?

266
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:47,320
Makes sense.

267
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:49,320
People always like to eat.

268
00:11:51,320 --> 00:11:53,320
Great value! Top quality!

269
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:56,320
This is one unique Okonomiyaki!

270
00:11:56,320 --> 00:11:58,320
Check it! Tomaki opened an Okonomiyaki booth.

271
00:11:58,320 --> 00:12:00,320
